# Documentation & Engineering Standards

- **Zero Placeholders:** Never use `# <insert config here>`, `TODO`, or ellipses (`...`). Every YAML manifest, cURL command, and Python script must be fully populated and syntactically valid.
- **Dual-Audience Separation:**
  - Files under `docs/executive/` must focus on business value, TCO savings of zero-replica failover, SLA tiers, and high-level Mermaid architecture diagrams.
  - Files under `docs/model-serving/`, `docs/gpu-partitioning/`, and `docs/platform-prerequisites/` must provide verbatim CLI commands and production Kubernetes manifests.
- **High Availability Mandates:**
  - Single-replica flagship model must specify 10s eviction tolerations for `node.kubernetes.io/not-ready` and `node.kubernetes.io/unreachable`.
  - Use `flagship-critical-priority` (value: 1000000000) with `PreemptLowerPriority`.
  - Model storage mounts must strictly use CephFS `ReadWriteMany` (RWX) PVCs.
- **MkDocs Strict Compliance:** All markdown links must resolve locally to prevent broken references during `mkdocs build --strict`.
